<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dinguiraye</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dinguiraye is a town in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a>, on the edge of the Futa Jallon highlands. In 1849 the Tijani scholar Umar Tall established a fortified base there, where he trained followers and gathered firearms before launching in 1852 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihad</a> that created the Toucouleur Empire. It remained an important religious centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tijaniyya">Tijaniyya</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dinguiraye.jpg" alt="Dinguiraye" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guinea_Dinguiraye_market.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
